From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kai Krakow <kai@kaishome.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:32:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvkms: drop the default for the removed SST EDID recovery
 regkey

"nvkms: enable the DisplayPort SST EDID recovery fix by default" makes
EvoInterface::getRegkeyValue() return 1 for
DP_ENABLE_SST_EDID_RECOVERY_FIX. The DP library no longer reads that
key: 620.70.06 removed NV_DP_REGKEY_ENABLE_SST_EDID_RECOVERY_FIX and
bEnableSstEdidRecoveryFix from dp_regkeydatabase.h and from the regkey
table in dp_evoadapter.cpp, and the three places that checked it now
always take the fixed path:

- dp_sst_edid.cpp clears the patched checksum flag before every re-read
- dp_sst_edid.cpp retries a read with an invalid EDID header
- Edid::swap() in dp_edid.cpp swaps the forced, fallback and patched
  flags together with the data

The behaviour the patch enabled is the upstream default since 620.70.06,
and the key is never queried, so the default is dead code. Remove it,
which restores getRegkeyValue() to its upstream form.

Fixes: 192e8e64bbfb ("nvkms: enable the DisplayPort SST EDID recovery fix by default")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/src/dp/nvdp-evo-interface.cpp | 15 ++-------------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/dp/nvdp-evo-interface.cpp b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/dp/nvdp-evo-interface.cpp
index ac1ae177..fa7e823b 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/src/dp/nvdp-evo-interface.cpp
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/src/dp/nvdp-evo-interface.cpp
@@ -80,20 +80,9 @@ NvU32 EvoInterface::getRegkeyValue(const char *key)
 
     if (found) {
         return val;
+    } else {
+        return 0;
     }
-
-    //
-    // NVKMS registry keys only come from clients that pass them at device
-    // allocation (the X driver); nvidia-drm passes none. Without the SST EDID
-    // recovery fix, one corrupted EDID block (e.g. an eDP panel read right
-    // after resume) leaves the EDID marked as patched through every re-read,
-    // and the DP library reports its fallback EDID instead of the panel's.
-    //
-    if (nvkms_strcmp(key, "DP_ENABLE_SST_EDID_RECOVERY_FIX") == 0) {
-        return 1;
-    }
-
-    return 0;
 }
 
 bool EvoInterface::isInbandStereoSignalingSupported()
